fix(home): per-bucket body copy on Slab B (hoodies vs headwear)

Slab B picks whichever non-tee bucket is biggest, but the body paragraph was
hard-coded "Heavyweight, slow-burn pieces for late nights at the wheel." That
line only fits hoodies. When headwear had more pieces it became the secondary
drop and the user saw a giant "Crown the work." headline followed by hoodie
language - words that don't make sense for caps and beanies.

Each candidate now carries its own body string, so the copy stays on-brand
whether hoodies or headwear is the secondary drop:
- Hoodies: "Heavyweight, slow-burn pieces for late nights at the wheel."
- Headwear: "Low-profile caps and beanies built to wear in, not break in."
